    "created_at": "2026-01-23T04:17:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-23T04:18:04Z",
    "body": "`0xWS` is leftover from a time before the \"Leading Bytes to Be Ignored\" column was added to tables in 3ac32c17d407f9f21bcc16c504d8e68491155d34. It is no longer used directly as an abbreviation, except in the definition.\n\n`0xTT` is, however, still used. Values in the \"Byte Pattern\" and \"Pattern Mask\" columns of tables are shown without the `0x` prefix because it makes copying and pasting easier; it is implied for those values.",
